dia" title="Vox Media" id="mwEs0">Vox Media</a>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20171011074252/https://www.theverge.com/circuitbreaker/2017/10/4/16408962/new-google-pixel-2-phone-announced-price-release-date-features" class="external text" id="mwEs4">Archived</a> from the original on October 11, 2017<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwEs8">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwEtA">October 12,</span> 2017</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Verge&amp;rft.atitle=Google+Pixel+2+and+2+XL+announced+with+water+resistance%2C+%27dual-pixel%27+camera%2C+and+always-on+display&amp;rft.date=2017-10-04&amp;rft.aulast=Kastrenakes&amp;rft.aufirst=Jacob&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theverge.com%2Fcircuitbreaker%2F2017%2F10%2F4%2F16408962%2Fnew-google-pixel-2-phone-announced-price-release-date-features&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AAndroid+%28operating+system%29" class="Z3988" about="#mwt251" id="mwEtE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-78" id="cite_note-78" data-mw-footnote-number="76"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEtI"><a href="#cite_ref-78" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEtM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEtQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-78" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt254" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwEtU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite news","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://www.theverge.com/2019/5/19/18631558/google-huawei-android-suspension"},"title":{"wt":"Google pulls Huawei&apos;s Android license, forcing it to use open source version"},"last1":{"wt":"Sottek"},"first1":{"wt":"T.C."},"date":{"wt":"May 19, 2019"},"work":{"wt":"[[The Verge]]"},"access-date":{"wt":"July 20, 2019"},"publisher":{"wt":"[[VOX Media]]"},"quote":{"wt":"A dramatic escalation in the US war on Chinese tech firms"},"archive-date":{"wt":"May 20, 2019"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20190520153127/https://www.theverge.com/2019/5/19/18631558/google-huawei-android-suspension"},"url-status":{"wt":"live"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFSottek2019" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt254">Sottek, T.C. (May 19, 2019). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.theverge.com/2019/5/19/18631558/google-huawei-android-suspension" class="external text" id="mwEtY">"Google pulls Huawei's Android license, forcing it to use open source version"</a>. <i id="mwEtc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Verge" title="The Verge" id="mwEtg">The Verge</a></i>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VOX_Media" title="VOX Media" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEtk">VOX Media</a>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20190520153127/https://www.theverge.com/2019/5/19/18631558/google-huawei-android-suspension" class="external text" id="mwEto">Archived</a> from the original on May 20, 2019<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwEts">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwEtw">July 20,</span> 2019</span>. <q id="mwEt0">A dramatic escalation in the US war on Chinese tech firms</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Verge&amp;rft.atitle=Google+pulls+Huawei%27s+Android+license%2C+forcing+it+to+use+open+source+version&amp;rft.date=2019-05-19&amp;rft.aulast=Sottek&amp;rft.aufirst=T.C.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theverge.com%2F2019%2F5%2F19%2F18631558%2Fgoogle-huawei-android-suspension&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AAndroid+%28operating+system%29" class="Z3988" about="#mwt254" id="mwEt4"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-79" id="cite_note-79" data-mw-footnote-number="77"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEt8"><a href="#cite_ref-79" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEuA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEuE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-79" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt257" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwEuI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite news","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/technology/2019/05/20/google-restricts-huawei-using-android-could-mean/"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220110/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/technology/2019/05/20/google-restricts-huawei-using-android-could-mean/"},"archive-date":{"wt":"January 10, 2022"},"url-access":{"wt":"subscription"},"url-status":{"wt":"live"},"title":{"wt":"Google restricts Huawei from using Android: Here&apos;s what that could mean for you"},"last1":{"wt":"Cook"},"first1":{"wt":"James"},"date":{"wt":"May 20, 2019"},"work":{"wt":"[[The Daily Telegraph|The Telegraph]]"},"access-date":{"wt":"July 20, 2019"},"department":{"wt":"Technology Intelligence"},"quote":{"wt":"Huawei, which is the world&apos;s second largest seller of smartphones after Samsung, has long relied on Google&apos;s Android operating system to run its smartphones and tablets. The ban means that new Huawei phones will no longer be able to access certain apps, such as Google Maps and YouTube, and existing phones will not be able to update their Android operating systems."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFCook2019" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt257">Cook, James (May 20, 2019). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwEuM"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.telegraph.co.uk/technology/2019/05/20/google-restricts-huawei-using-android-could-mean/" class="external text" id="mwEuQ">"Google restricts Huawei from using Android: Here's what that could mean for you"</a></span>. Technology Intelligence. <i id="mwEuU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Daily_Telegraph" title="The Daily Telegraph" id="mwEuY">The Telegraph</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220110/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/technology/2019/05/20/google-restricts-huawei-using-android-could-mean/" class="external text" id="mwEuc">Archived</a> from the original on January 10, 2022<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwEug">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwEuk">July 20,</span> 2019</span>. <q id="mwEuo">Huawei, which is the world's second largest seller of smartphones after Samsung, has long relied on Google's Android operating system to run its smartphones and tablets. The ban means that new Huawei phones will no longer be able to access certain apps, such as Google Maps and YouTube, and existing phones will not be able to update their Android operating systems.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Telegraph&amp;rft.atitle=Google+restricts+Huawei+from+using+Android%3A+Here%27s+what+that+could+mean+for+you&amp;rft.date=2019-05-20&amp;rft.aulast=Cook&amp;rft.aufirst=James&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.telegraph.co.uk%2Ftechnology%2F2019%2F05%2F20%2Fgoogle-restricts-huawei-using-android-could-mean%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AAndroid+%28operating+system%29" class="Z3988" about="#mwt257" id="mwEus"></span><span about="#mwt259" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEuw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cbignore","href":"./Template:Cbignore"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></span></span></li>
